    "isDraft": false,
    "number": 154,
    "title": "feat(blender): typed GLB export and owner-pinned runtime",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T08:32:19Z",
    "url": "https://github.com/seradotcom/semwright/pull/154",
    "baseRefName": "main",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nThis makes the Blender to game-engine asset handoff a first-party typed Semwright capability and removes ambient Blender executable discovery from the deep driver.\n\n### Typed GLB handoff\n\nAdds blender.export.glb / driver.blender.export.glb.\n\nThe operation:\n- exports one exact named collection;\n- emits a self-contained GLB 2.0 artifact;\n- accepts only meshes, armatures and empties;\n- requires parents and armature dependencies to remain inside the collection;\n- preserves Blender selection and active-object state;\n- uses a private temporary file plus no-clobber publication;\n- refuses overwrite, path escape and symbolic output targets;\n- validates the GLB header and a bounded artifact size;\n- returns relative path, SHA-256, bytes and exported object count;\n- is tagged artifact-out:model/3d;\n- does not expose generic bpy.ops, Python eval/exec or arbitrary operator invocation.\n\n### Owner-pinned Blender runtime\n\nThe deep driver no longer searches /usr/bin, /usr/local/bin or ambient PATH.\n\nIt now requires:\n- read-only blender-runtime mount containing Blender 4.5.14 LTS resources/libraries;\n- blender-executable tool authority for the exact Blender ELF, pinned by SHA-256 and materialized by Driver Host as /plugin/tools/blender.\n\nStartup verifies the portable runtime layout and requires exactly Blender 4.5.14 LTS.\n\n### CI / integration coverage added\n\nThe Blender native-integration job is updated to exercise:\n- official Blender 4.5.14 archive verification;\n- real typed GLB adapter contract;\n- portable runtime plus /plugin/tools/blender Bubblewrap preflight;\n- Landlock startup with only explicit runtime/tool roots;\n- real DriverProvider GLB export, SHA verification and no-overwrite;\n- broker/CLI GLB export;\n- existing render/save and interactive add-on coverage.\n\n## Local work performed\n\nPer project strategy, no heavy Rust compilation/tests were run locally. Only cheap source sanity checks were run:\n- cargo fmt --all -- --check\n- generated contract sync check\n- JSON validation\n- Bash syntax\n- Python AST parsing\n- git diff --check\n\nHeavy verification is intentionally delegated to GitHub Actions.\n",
